            "id": "8bb62baf-41b7-3ea5-8984-db10b4deb39e",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "This Surging Stock Could Have More Upside as SpaceX Moves Toward a Possible 2026 IPO",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Surging  EchoStar  stock could have more upside if SpaceX ends up going public in 2026 at anything close to the reported $1.5 trillion valuation that the Elon Musk-controlled satellite, rocket, and space company could seek.  EchoStar has become the top SpaceX proxy in the public markets since EchoStar sold wireless spectrum to SpaceX in two separate transactions in September and November for a package of cash and SpaceX stock.  EchoStar stock has more than tripled since the initial transaction in September, and the shares have gained 27% to $104.39 this week after Bloomberg reported that SpaceX could seek a $1.5 trillion valuation\u2014the largest of any private company\u2014in a potential 2026 IPO.",
            "pubDate": "2025-12-11T23:32:00Z",
            "displayTime": "2025-12-11T23:32:00Z",
            "isHosted": false,
            "bypassModal": false,
